  "id": "eval.2026-07-29-eval-202743.sandboxed-tool-fleet",
  "title": "2026-07-29-eval-202743 · sandboxed-tool-fleet",
  "description": "# Sandboxed tool-execution fleet\n\nA left-to-right operational map of disposable environments used by tool-calling agents. Requests pass through tenant concurrency and aggregate-runtime admission, then take either an immediate compatible warm-pool hit or a capacity-aware cold boot on a healthy host.\n\nThe center follows each environment through provisioning, ready, leased, idle, draining, and destroyed. Renewal heartbeats preserve a fixed-term lease; lease expiry or absolute maximum age invokes the reclaimer, which destroys the environment and never returns prior-tenant state to the pool. Image retirement drains old instances and waits for active work before destruction.\n\nWithin a lease, each tool call is governed by timeout, memory, CPU, and allowlisted proxy egress controls. Output is capped and streamed; durable session-keyed files go to the artifact store because local state is ephemeral. The pool supervisor adjusts pre-booted supply from capacity and demand, repeated boot failures quarantine hosts, and operations track boot latency, reclamations, timeouts, and escape-attempt signals.",
  "mode": "diagram",
